[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. The reports say otherwise. Dates went wrong for
**two different reasons**, and the queued fix covered one of them.

<Callout>
Not one known issue. Two problems, each with its own ticket.
</Callout>

## The two problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| ticket | problem | what happens |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [#1](https://github.com/nifesimii/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/1) | `parser` | The shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped. |
| [#2](https://github.com/nifesimii/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/2) | `hint` | booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Day-first tenants type what it says, and the form reads it day first. |

The numbers above are computed from the export, not typed. Each report is counted once, where the
desk files it.

<SubjectSpread ticket={4471} />

## How we told them apart

A report's cause depends on its tenant: the locale it writes dates in, and the booking form it
runs. The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The table shows how far it is off:
intake tagged some `parser` reports `hint`, and some `hint` reports `parser`.

## The one-day reports

The desk's notes mark some reports as a one-day move (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`). Read them:
"Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May", "Every booking in June is one day off", "Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday". The desk counts them under `parser`, where their
tenant files them, and footnotes them under the table. We keep that count. We also note that none
of them swaps a month and a day, and some mention two places. If someone fixes the parser and these
reports keep coming, look at time zones next. The export cannot prove it either way.

## What the subject line hid

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. The note under
the table counts the subject lines that appear under both causes: most of them do. A subject says how
a person felt about the bug. It does not say which bug it is. This is why two problems ended up as
one ticket.

## What happened

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October.

- `parser`: fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). #1 is closed.
- `hint`: won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired. #2 is closed.

Still open for the desk:

- Replace decision 0001 with a new record. Do not edit it: accepted records are never edited.
- Until then, do not merge a report on its subject line alone. Check the tenant and the channel.
- If one-day reports keep coming after the parser fix, look at time zones.

## Check my work

- Four `parser` reports (R-41290, R-41417, R-41514, R-41615) do not name a date pair. They are filed under `parser` because of their tenant, as `causes.ts` says.
- The `hint` reports all come through the form channel, from three tenants: Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.

